      "message": "Fixed and working. `slugify` no longer produces repeated dashes.\n\nThe bug was in `slug/core.py`: every non-alphanumeric character became a `-` with no check on the previous character, so `\"Hello -- World\"` came out as `hello---world`. The fix only adds a dash when the last character written wasn't already one. I also strip trailing dashes, so `\"Hi!!\"` gives `hi` rather than `hi-`.\n\nSpot-check results:\n- `'Hello -- World'` → `hello-world`\n- `'a   b'` → `a-b`\n- `'  Hi!!  there '` → `hi-there`\n- `'Hello World'` → `hello-world` (the existing test case's input)\n\nI didn't run the test suite, as you asked. The spot-check was a single quick run.",
